meta {
  name: Server Details
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/method/implementor.client_api.get_server?server=s6qivo97hn
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  server: s6qivo97hn
  ~customer: Hamza
}

tests {
  test("returns 200", function () {
    expect(res.status).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("has message", function () {
    expect(res.body).to.have.property("message");
  });

  test("specs come as fields and versions are flat", function () {
    const s = res.body.message;
    ["cpu", "memory_gb", "storage_gb", "storage_type", "os"].forEach(function (k) {
      expect(s.specs).to.have.property(k);
    });
    expect(s).to.have.property("erpnext_version");
    expect(s).to.have.property("frappe_version");
    expect(s).to.not.have.property("versions");
    expect(s.activity).to.be.an("array");
  });
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  One server: everything from Servers, plus specs, versions and recent activity.

  **Endpoint:** `GET /api/method/implementor.client_api.get_server`  
  **Screen:** Hosting detail

  **Permission:** Signed-in client user (Client User or Client Admin). Only records of the user's own client company are returned.

  **Query parameters:**

  | Field | Type | Required | Example | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `server` | string | yes | `s6qivo97hn` | `name` from Servers. |
  | `customer` | string | no | `Hamza` | Not used by the app. The server picks the user's company. Disabled by default. |

  **Response:** every field of a Servers item (including `backup_frequency` and `backup_retention`), plus the ones below.

  ```json
  {
    "message": {
      "name": "s6qivo97hn",
      "server_name": "hamza-erp-prod",
      "site_url": "erp.hamza.sa",
      "status": "online",
      "erpnext_version": "v15.40.0",
      "frappe_version": "v15.45.2",
      "...": "... the other Servers fields ...",
      "specs": {
        "cpu": "4 OCPU (Ampere A1)",
        "memory_gb": 24,
        "storage_gb": 200,
        "storage_type": "Block Volume",
        "os": "Ubuntu 22.04 LTS"
      },
      "specs_text": "4 OCPU (Ampere A1)\n24 GB RAM\n200 GB Block Volume\nUbuntu 22.04 LTS",
      "activity": [
        {
          "activity_type": "restore",
          "date": "2026-10-15T22:00:00+03:00",
          "downtime_window": "22:00–22:30",
          "workflow_state": "done"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```

  **Fields:**

  - `erpnext_version`, `frappe_version`: flat fields. There is no `versions` object. Either can be null.
  - `specs`: read from the server's spec text. Always an object.
    - `cpu`: text, e.g. "4 OCPU (Ampere A1)".
    - `memory_gb`, `storage_gb`: numbers in GB (TB values are converted).
    - `storage_type`: text after the size on the storage line, e.g. "Block Volume" from "200 GB Block Volume". Null when there is none.
    - `os`: text.
    - Any of them is null if it couldn't be read; show `specs_text` instead then.
  - `specs_text`: the original text, with line breaks. Null when no specs were entered (then every `specs` field is null).
  - `activity[]`: up to 20 recent events, newest first. Can be empty.
    - `activity_type`: lowercase code: `provisioning`, `upgrade`, `update`, `restore` or `scaling`.
    - `date`: date-time with offset.
    - `downtime_window`: free text, e.g. "22:00–22:30". Can be null.
    - `workflow_state`: lowercase code: `requested`, `scheduled`, `in_maintenance`, `verified` or `done`. Can be null.

  **Errors:** client API errors have an `error_code`. Auth errors come from Frappe and have none.

  - **401** (no error_code): token expired or invalid. Refresh once and retry, else sign out.
  - **403** (no error_code): no Authorization header sent.
  - **403** `not_permitted`: not this client's server, or the server doesn't exist.
  - **403** `no_client_linked`: the user isn't linked to any client company.
  - **417** `missing_parameter`: `server` left out.
}
